      "writtenOn": "2025-08-13T05:55:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027ve gone through the code grepping it and checking how drm_bridge is being used - it seems that drivers which utilize drm_bridge are calling kzalloc. I didn\u0027t notice any usage that could end in falling into the `support_hdcp \u003d true` because of some garbage memory. Also there are other booleans, like \u0027pre_enable_prev_first\u0027 or `interlace_allowed` and these are not explicitly zeroed in any driver during the initialization. I\u0027d expect these also rely on the assumption that drm_bridge structure (even when wrapped in another struct) will be kzalloc\u0027ed.",
      "parentUuid": "3408cc01_c4faeaa9",
